WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:04.810
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

00:04.810 --> 00:12.540
Asano hitogomi o nagamete coffee nondeiru
Watching a crowd in the morning, and drinking coffee

00:13.450 --> 00:21.450
Aseri nado naikano youni hitoni wa mieru daro
People must see me as if I don't have any worries

00:22.080 --> 00:29.920
lma menomae ni atomodori dekinai jikan ga
I know that the time I will never be able to get back

00:30.710 --> 00:38.220
Tashika ni nagareteru koto o watashi wa shitteru
Is moving in front of me

00:38.440 --> 00:47.440
Marude kyou shika nai toiu ikikata o shitemita toki
If I live like today is the last day of my life

00:47.730 --> 00:55.480
Saisho ni nani ga mieru darou
I wonder what I can see first

00:56.590 --> 01:00.830
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:01.260 --> 01:09.260
Sore ga donnani chiisana hikari demo ii
I don't care no matter how small the light is

01:09.770 --> 01:11.750
Sugata o misete hoshii
I just wish to see its shape

01:11.750 --> 01:16.010
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:16.680 --> 01:22.470
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.470 --> 01:22.680
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.680 --> 01:29.190
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest
Sonna hito ni deaitai
Who I can tell my honest feelings to

01:29.190 --> 01:30.980
Mermaid Forest
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology

01:37.490 --> 01:41.990
Episode 11
Promised Tomorrow
(Part II)

01:53.110 --> 01:54.580
Stop it!

02:01.290 --> 02:03.410
Run, Yuta!

02:16.700 --> 02:17.630
Yuta!

02:21.870 --> 02:22.810
Yuta!

02:23.210 --> 02:24.540
Are you still alive?

02:27.410 --> 02:29.680
I have no time to be dying now.

02:34.350 --> 02:36.880
<i>I have to find Mana</i>
<i>before Eijiro does...</i>

02:37.260 --> 02:38.450
<i>or she'll be in danger.</i>

02:58.210 --> 02:58.910
This way!

02:58.910 --> 02:59.810
Don't let them get away!

03:04.420 --> 03:05.820
They're coming!
Come on!

03:06.950 --> 03:07.750
There they are!

03:12.260 --> 03:13.420
Not this way.

03:15.390 --> 03:16.830
The Red Valley.

03:17.760 --> 03:18.860
I have to go back.

03:20.170 --> 03:21.660
No way, we can't go there!

03:21.870 --> 03:22.830
Hurry!

03:36.620 --> 03:39.050
We won't be able to see Yuta
if they catch us.

03:39.520 --> 03:41.610
I promised Yuta
I'll be waiting...

03:42.190 --> 03:44.160
for him in the Red Valley.

03:45.120 --> 03:47.020
I've already heard
that many times.

03:47.430 --> 03:48.220
Hurry up!

03:49.060 --> 03:50.590
I promised...

03:50.830 --> 03:51.800
A promise...

03:55.730 --> 03:59.100
If I'd gone to the Red Valley
on that day...

03:59.910 --> 04:00.960
That's right.

04:01.570 --> 04:04.340
If you couldn't go,
why did you promise her?

04:05.080 --> 04:07.380
Why did you give her the signal?

04:07.880 --> 04:09.810
I told you, I didn't promise...

04:11.720 --> 04:12.410
The signal?

04:12.720 --> 04:14.480
Don't tell me you've forgotten.

04:15.090 --> 04:18.150
It's the signal that
Miss Nae and you were using.

04:22.530 --> 04:24.000
<i>We line three stones like this...</i>

04:24.000 --> 04:26.460
<i>behind the statue of</i>
<i>the travelers' guardian deity.</i>

04:26.830 --> 04:27.990
<i>If I can see him...</i>

04:28.400 --> 04:30.800
<i>I take away the middle stone</i>
<i>and he does the same.</i>

04:31.300 --> 04:32.570
<i>If we can't...</i>

04:32.840 --> 04:34.030
<i>we leave it where it is.</i>

04:34.570 --> 04:35.670
<i>Sokichi...</i>

04:36.940 --> 04:40.040
<i>I'm going to go with Yuta.</i>

04:40.750 --> 04:42.110
<i>We promised.</i>

04:44.250 --> 04:47.920
Miss Nae clearly said that
you two made a promise...

04:47.920 --> 04:49.410
and that you gave her the signal.

04:49.790 --> 04:51.020
I didn't.

04:52.890 --> 04:55.420
Did someone else do it?

04:55.890 --> 04:57.330
It's a small village.

04:57.760 --> 05:01.100
It's no surprise if someone
figured out the signal.

05:01.900 --> 05:04.530
<i>Then Nae went to</i>
<i>the Red Valley...</i>

05:04.800 --> 05:07.240
<i>believing the false signal</i>
<i>to be from me.</i>

05:10.980 --> 05:13.410
Please hurry up,
I'm buying this.

05:16.650 --> 05:17.510
Damn.

05:17.650 --> 05:19.550
They've run off into
a hard place to find.

05:30.000 --> 05:30.930
What?

05:34.830 --> 05:36.100
This is pretty.

05:36.570 --> 05:37.660
I wonder...

05:38.300 --> 05:39.700
if Yuta will like it.

05:48.210 --> 05:48.840
Let's go!

05:49.750 --> 05:51.150
Ah, miss...

05:51.720 --> 05:53.550
They'll pay for it.

06:01.060 --> 06:02.150
That car...

06:09.640 --> 06:11.130
It's Eijiro's.

06:12.500 --> 06:13.300
Let's go.

06:24.150 --> 06:25.080
This way.

06:25.520 --> 06:27.310
The shape of that mountain...

06:27.420 --> 06:28.440
Is that the Red Valley?

06:28.650 --> 06:29.950
A little farther...

06:30.320 --> 06:31.410
Soon...

06:39.600 --> 06:40.460
What's the matter?

06:48.110 --> 06:49.230
Are you scared?

06:50.710 --> 06:52.010
They're just birds.

06:55.050 --> 06:56.240
Nae...

06:58.820 --> 06:59.680
You old bastard!

07:00.950 --> 07:03.610
I didn't want to believe
you'd come here.

07:04.990 --> 07:06.180
I didn't want to believe...

07:07.590 --> 07:09.790
you'd really come here.

07:13.470 --> 07:16.130
Let's go home, Nae.

07:17.040 --> 07:20.060
You're not capable
of living in the outside world.

07:23.240 --> 07:24.940
Come, Nae.

07:25.210 --> 07:26.910
No, Master!

07:27.350 --> 07:30.510
She loses herself
when she hears the birds.

07:30.820 --> 07:32.810
She wouldn't harm me.

07:34.020 --> 07:34.820
Come.

07:35.820 --> 07:36.690
No.

07:50.570 --> 07:51.700
Nae...

07:52.170 --> 07:53.430
You...

07:54.170 --> 07:56.270
How could you...

07:59.980 --> 08:00.950
Master.

08:01.710 --> 08:05.550
I brought your dead body
back to life...

08:05.550 --> 08:07.380
with the mermaid ash!

08:13.130 --> 08:14.320
Nae...

08:20.370 --> 08:21.920
What are you doing?

08:22.870 --> 08:25.130
Get rid of them quickly.

08:25.500 --> 08:26.530
But...

08:27.040 --> 08:29.770
You've been giving us
strict orders not to harm Miss...

08:30.440 --> 08:33.210
They're monsters!

08:33.510 --> 08:35.780
They should not be allowed to live.

08:40.420 --> 08:41.480
Damn!

08:41.650 --> 08:45.210
I was younger than you
60 years ago.

08:45.690 --> 08:46.680
I'm going ahead.

08:47.230 --> 08:48.190
This way, right?

08:49.090 --> 08:50.790
Wait. Wait for me!

08:51.060 --> 08:53.120
I want to take part
in rescuing Miss Nae.

08:53.530 --> 08:55.630
I don't know
what's going on...

08:56.100 --> 08:57.530
but I want to rescue her!

09:06.410 --> 09:07.710
The Red Valley...

09:08.050 --> 09:09.100
Soon...

09:09.580 --> 09:10.680
Yuta.

09:10.680 --> 09:11.840
Stop right there!

09:12.150 --> 09:13.910
You won't get away,
you little wenches!

09:15.590 --> 09:16.450
But...

09:16.620 --> 09:18.420
If it wasn't you...

09:18.420 --> 09:20.120
who gave that signal?

09:21.260 --> 09:22.620
Eijiro, wasn't it?

09:23.060 --> 09:25.200
I thought so first, too...

09:25.200 --> 09:26.690
but don't you find it strange?

09:26.830 --> 09:27.760
What is?

09:27.900 --> 09:31.030
It was his fiancée who was trying
to elope with someone else.

09:31.170 --> 09:33.470
It'd make more sense
if he'd returned the stone...

09:33.470 --> 09:35.800
to prevent her from
going to the Red Valley...

09:36.240 --> 09:38.470
but what he actually did
was call her there.

09:38.910 --> 09:40.480
Had he not done anything...

09:40.480 --> 09:42.500
you'd just have left
the village by yourself.

09:45.120 --> 09:46.740
Let go!

09:48.320 --> 09:49.310
Ouch!

09:49.790 --> 09:50.760
You brat!

09:55.730 --> 09:57.630
Go ahead! Now!

09:58.100 --> 09:59.260
To the Red Valley!

10:01.500 --> 10:02.360
Go!

10:04.700 --> 10:05.830
<i>Yuta...</i>

10:06.340 --> 10:07.430
<i>Yuta...</i>

10:20.010 --> 10:30.020
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest

10:39.400 --> 10:40.800
Nae...

10:55.650 --> 10:56.810
Nae...

10:57.320 --> 10:58.620
You old bastard!

11:01.660 --> 11:02.520
Cut her...

11:04.100 --> 11:05.220
head off!

11:19.180 --> 11:20.080
Bastards!

11:21.110 --> 11:21.910
Yuta!

11:21.980 --> 11:22.580
Mana!

11:22.580 --> 11:23.410
Yuta!

11:24.980 --> 11:27.040
You're still alive.

11:29.020 --> 11:31.650
Eijiro, it was you, wasn't it...

11:32.060 --> 11:35.620
who tricked Nae into coming to
the Red Valley that day?

11:44.270 --> 11:47.570
<i>Nae. Yuta's not coming.</i>

11:50.540 --> 11:51.800
<i>Eijiro.</i>

11:52.840 --> 11:55.400
<i>You followed me.</i>

11:56.080 --> 11:57.050
<i>Nae...</i>

11:58.350 --> 12:00.550
<i>I didn't want to believe</i>
<i>you'd come here.</i>

12:01.320 --> 12:04.520
<i>I didn't want to believe</i>
<i>you'd really come here.</i>

12:05.660 --> 12:07.120
<i>What do you mean?</i>

12:07.730 --> 12:10.790
<i>I'm the one who moved</i>
<i>the signal stone.</i>

12:11.430 --> 12:13.950
<i>But I wanted to believe</i>
<i>that you wouldn't come.</i>

12:15.470 --> 12:17.730
<i>I wanted to believe</i>
<i>that you'd never come.</i>

12:28.650 --> 12:29.980
<i>In the Red Valley...</i>

12:30.720 --> 12:32.150
<i>With Yuta...</i>

12:52.440 --> 12:53.700
<i>The Red Valley.</i>

12:54.970 --> 12:57.810
<i>If you want to leave the village,</i>
<i>I'll take you.</i>

12:57.810 --> 12:59.670
<i>No, please stop it!</i>

13:04.180 --> 13:08.140
<i>Yes...I was killed then.</i>

13:13.060 --> 13:15.960
<i>Yuta didn't come.</i>

13:17.200 --> 13:19.160
<i>I was killed here.</i>

13:20.830 --> 13:24.930
<i>Yuta didn't come.</i>

13:27.140 --> 13:28.970
Were you planning to kill her?

13:29.270 --> 13:32.710
Did you lure Miss Nae out
to kill her from the beginning?

13:33.450 --> 13:35.440
Of course not.

13:36.950 --> 13:41.580
If only Nae had
reconsidered right then...

13:43.520 --> 13:44.550
<i>Nae.</i>

13:45.260 --> 13:46.380
<i>It's all right.</i>

13:47.090 --> 13:48.250
<i>It's all right.</i>

13:50.060 --> 13:52.090
<i>I'll bring you back to life soon.</i>

13:52.860 --> 13:54.830
<i>I'll sprinkle</i>
<i>the mermaid ash over you.</i>

13:57.470 --> 14:01.370
But you couldn't find
the mermaid ash.

14:03.070 --> 14:07.480
Flowers were in full bloom
all year long in the field...

14:08.210 --> 14:11.110
where Nae had scattered the
mermaid ash out of mischief.

14:11.880 --> 14:14.220
<i>No, Nae...</i>

14:14.890 --> 14:17.790
<i>humans aren't supposed to use</i>
<i>things that came from a mermaid.</i>

14:18.660 --> 14:20.650
<i>You think so?</i>

14:21.460 --> 14:24.490
<i>Well, if you say so, Yuta...</i>

14:24.760 --> 14:27.600
<i>I'll hide it somewhere</i>
<i>without telling my father.</i>

14:28.900 --> 14:30.940
The mermaid ash...

14:30.940 --> 14:35.000
I'd believed to be in
the storehouse was gone.

14:35.910 --> 14:38.000
To be honest, I panicked.

14:38.480 --> 14:43.070
Because if I didn't do anything,
I'd be a murderer.

14:43.720 --> 14:46.810
Eijiro, didn't you know...

14:47.620 --> 14:49.610
the secret legend
of the mermaid ash?

14:51.220 --> 14:53.590
The murdered traveling nun
came back to life...

14:53.590 --> 14:56.150
because of the mermaid ash
that remained on her dead body...

14:56.930 --> 14:59.120
she turned into
a soulless demon and...

14:59.660 --> 15:02.160
went on killing
one villager after another.

15:03.800 --> 15:05.960
Of course I knew the legend.

15:06.340 --> 15:07.360
But...

15:08.140 --> 15:13.480
if Nae is soulless,
I can do as I please with her.

15:14.350 --> 15:15.400
You...

15:16.780 --> 15:18.150
It took such a long time.

15:19.180 --> 15:21.210
Until I finished purchasing
all the land and...

15:21.320 --> 15:24.020
found the mermaid ash at last...

15:24.760 --> 15:30.220
I could not feel
at ease even for one day.

15:31.200 --> 15:33.130
Finally, two years ago...

15:33.130 --> 15:37.030
I found the mermaid ash
buried in a mountain.

15:38.070 --> 15:43.200
Miraculously, Nae's body buried
in the flower field was not rotten...

15:43.810 --> 15:46.680
and she was extremely beautiful.

15:48.150 --> 15:53.350
<i>Nae, here, the mermaid ash.</i>

16:07.670 --> 16:11.000
But I was wrong.

16:11.970 --> 16:14.130
That's not Nae.

16:14.970 --> 16:19.340
That's a soulless demon,
after all.

16:19.640 --> 16:20.510
No!

16:20.850 --> 16:21.540
Mana.

16:21.850 --> 16:24.180
She remembers Yuta!

16:24.650 --> 16:26.410
She said they promised!

16:29.250 --> 16:31.810
She's waiting for Yuta
in the Red Valley.

16:32.390 --> 16:33.020
Mana.

16:33.520 --> 16:35.490
She's waiting even now.

16:53.680 --> 16:57.170
Hey, you might get killed as well.

16:57.880 --> 17:00.370
Doesn't matter, he'll come back
to life right away anyway.

17:00.990 --> 17:02.820
How do you know?

17:03.220 --> 17:06.990
Even if you see her,
she doesn't have a soul.

17:07.460 --> 17:09.320
She's an empty shell.

17:33.380 --> 17:34.250
Nae.

17:35.790 --> 17:38.280
Had I come here...

17:39.520 --> 17:41.250
to the Red Valley, on that day...

17:46.970 --> 17:47.830
I'm sorry.

17:55.540 --> 17:56.630
Yuta?

17:58.110 --> 17:59.370
I'm glad.

17:59.740 --> 18:00.840
I was having...

18:02.880 --> 18:05.250
a very scary dream.

18:06.550 --> 18:07.420
<i>Nae...</i>

18:09.390 --> 18:11.380
You wouldn't come, and...

18:11.890 --> 18:16.220
And I...

18:17.400 --> 18:21.260
Oh, I'm so glad it was a dream.

18:22.030 --> 18:23.090
I see.

18:24.140 --> 18:27.730
I'm sorry I'm late, Nae.

18:33.680 --> 18:34.470
Let's go.

18:34.850 --> 18:38.980
Let's leave this village
together, Nae.

18:42.320 --> 18:43.620
<i>You know what, Yuta?</i>

18:44.620 --> 18:47.560
<i>What do you think happened to</i>
<i>the nun who came back to life?</i>

18:48.560 --> 18:50.260
<i>She took refuge in a mountain...</i>

18:50.260 --> 18:52.560
<i>because the villagers were</i>
<i>so frightened of her.</i>

18:53.200 --> 18:56.830
<i>And after a few years, the effect</i>
<i>of the mermaid ash wore out and...</i>

18:56.830 --> 18:59.500
<i>she became a dead body again.</i>

19:08.180 --> 19:10.980
<i>They say you're looking</i>
<i>for a mermaid.</i>

19:11.880 --> 19:12.750
<i>No.</i>

19:13.020 --> 19:15.750
<i>I can't take you with me, Nae. I...</i>

19:16.590 --> 19:18.090
<i>We line three stones like this...</i>

19:18.090 --> 19:20.390
<i>behind the statue of</i>
<i>the travelers' guardian deity.</i>

19:20.790 --> 19:22.230
<i>If I can see him...</i>

19:22.360 --> 19:24.490
<i>I take away the middle stone</i>
<i>and he does the same.</i>

19:25.230 --> 19:26.530
<i>Mermaid ash?</i>

19:27.370 --> 19:28.400
<i>That's right.</i>

19:28.400 --> 19:31.130
<i>I'll tell you about it</i>
<i>just because it's you.</i>

19:31.940 --> 19:34.540
<i>My father said</i>
<i>it's a family secret...</i>

19:34.540 --> 19:35.940
<i>but I don't care.</i>

19:36.270 --> 19:40.210
<i>But in return,</i>
<i>you have to take me with you...</i>

19:40.210 --> 19:42.410
<i>when you go look</i>
<i>for a mermaid, OK?</i>

19:49.320 --> 19:50.150
<i>Nae...</i>

19:51.290 --> 19:54.160
<i>I couldn't either live...</i>

19:54.160 --> 19:55.590
<i>or die with you.</i>

19:58.200 --> 20:00.130
<i>I want to become</i>
<i>immortal like you.</i>

20:01.530 --> 20:03.470
<i>I want to go with you.</i>

20:06.370 --> 20:07.740
Miss Nae...

20:08.670 --> 20:09.970
Is she dead?

20:10.980 --> 20:13.500
It was a dead body to begin with.

20:14.080 --> 20:17.810
Besides, the statute of
limitations expired long ago.

20:22.290 --> 20:27.090
That's right, Miss Nae
was having a nightmare.

20:27.590 --> 20:29.990
But...but!

20:30.190 --> 20:32.990
What you did wasn't a dream!

20:40.470 --> 20:41.870
Damn!

21:13.070 --> 21:21.590
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

21:22.970 --> 21:31.470
ltsumade kakaruno to anata wa warau kedo
"How long does it take?" You smiled at me

21:32.930 --> 21:41.820
Dorekurai oboete iru hidoku naki nagara
How much do you remember? I cried hard

21:42.870 --> 21:52.370
Dorekurai oboete iru anokoto to ieba
How much do you remember if I talk about "that thing"?

21:57.460 --> 22:06.470
ltsumademo mada utsumuite
I still look down

22:07.430 --> 22:15.920
Tobikoe rarenai mizutamari
I can't jump over the puddle

22:17.070 --> 22:26.570
Wakaranakunaru moshikasuruto
I'm confused

22:26.910 --> 22:36.410
Kawarenai no wa watashi dake kana
Maybe I'm the only one who still can't change

22:41.380 --> 22:50.930
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

23:06.480 --> 23:09.680
Yuta, if you don't start moving
your butt, I'll leave you here.

23:10.020 --> 23:13.920
I couldn't care less whether
you come along or not.

23:20.000 --> 23:22.020
Are you jealous?

23:22.470 --> 23:23.990
You've matured a bit,
haven't you?

23:25.400 --> 23:26.700
Jealous?

23:27.370 --> 23:28.240
What's that?

23:28.370 --> 23:29.240
Does it taste good?

23:30.810 --> 23:32.710
I guess you're still a kid,
after all.

23:33.010 --> 23:34.380
Did you say something?

23:35.210 --> 23:37.200
No. Let's go.

23:39.320 --> 23:41.440
That's what I've been telling you!

23:43.590 --> 23:44.580
OK.

23:46.320 --> 23:48.450
<i>We still have a long way to go.</i>

23:49.230 --> 23:50.830
<i>Until the day comes...</i>

23:50.830 --> 23:54.700
<i>when we find the mermaid</i>
<i>who will grant my...our wish.</i>

23:55.900 --> 23:57.700
<i>Our journey goes on.</i>

23:59.170 --> 24:00.930
<i>It will continue on to</i>
<i>the end of the world.</i>

24:06.780 --> 24:09.010
We met a boy named Masato
during our journey two years ago.

24:09.480 --> 24:11.750
He told us that he was going to
live with his mother...

24:11.750 --> 24:12.950
then ran off from the station.

24:14.020 --> 24:17.450
But why does his mother
attack and hurt him?

24:17.960 --> 24:18.750
What?

24:18.960 --> 24:20.730
Masato's mother died
in an accident at sea...

24:20.730 --> 24:22.690
and then came back
to life the next day?

24:23.460 --> 24:25.450
Mana! It's a deformed one!

24:25.630 --> 24:28.030
